<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:14Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>US military cloud platform reportedly hacked as Pentagon insists systems are secure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65aff99df69a7a656098d12b6098a0a634ee196afccca9c1065b46e653e79374</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-28T06:04:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261128-us-military-cloud-platform-reportedly-hacked-as-pentagon-insists-systems-are-secure--de4a4715f23d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261128-us-military-cloud-platform-reportedly-hacked-as-pentagon-insists-systems-are-secure" /><summary type="html">Hackers reportedly breached the US Air Force's Cloud One platform late Friday, potentially exposing sensitive military data. The Pentagon did not specifically deny that the system had been accessed, but insists its networks remain secure amid an ongoing spate of cyber-related data incidents.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Back to Black Friday: 'We are now bombarded with offers throughout the year'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc494540cc385b9bde930e118ba0b9f855b13a3b6dff344f4961db3715a91451</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T15:53:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-black-friday-how-the-global-shopping-phenomenon-is-evolving-amid-the-cost-of-living-crisis--7abf501085a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-black-friday-how-the-global-shopping-phenomenon-is-evolving-amid-the-cost-of-living-crisis" /><summary type="html">Black Friday was once a single day of holiday sales, held the day after Thanksgiving. Then retailers began kicking things off a day early, on Thanksgiving itself. “We are now bombarded with offers throughout the year,” says Hilary Ingham, Professor of Economics and Department Head at Lancaster University, who has no plans to shop this Black Friday. Ingham acknowledges a growing sense of “retail fatigue” but still sees the potential for a peak in sales. Meanwhile, an investigation by The Telegraph suggests that six in ten of the most popular products were actually more expensive than earlier in the year, underscoring the need for consumers to remain vigilant and track prices over time.</summary></entry><entry><title>Almost a million Americans left without power on Thanksgiving as storm sweeps East Coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:644cf5a74d0cac74dc2f3687da3477561eeb50879742ed20492f07fd610c2442</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T07:14:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261127-almost-a-million-americans-left-without-power-on-thanksgiving-as-storm-sweeps-east-coast--28258dd11987.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261127-almost-a-million-americans-left-without-power-on-thanksgiving-as-storm-sweeps-east-coast" /><summary type="html">Nearly a million people were left without power Thursday after a severe storm lashed the East Coast of the US, tearing up trees and powerlines on Thanksgiving. New York City authorities had been forced to postpone the annual Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade due to the intense winds.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>In California, exceptional tides and nearly 9m-high waves batter the coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a2bca629d431b8e806e754dbe10cb8b48743c9f662b6fb482e45835572085a2</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T16:01:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261126-in-california-exceptional-tides-and-nearly-9m-high-waves-batter-the-coast--a64be760df29.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261126-in-california-exceptional-tides-and-nearly-9m-high-waves-batter-the-coast" /><summary type="html">USA: Powerful waves and king tides destroyed part of a pier in Pacifica, south of San Francisco, on Wednesday. In Marin County, authorities issued a temporary evacuation order and urged people to stay away from the beach.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Unacceptable': China, EU among major economies against new US tariffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a9d5dacb4fe6accf790a79780027c79b0ff5464aba8e208490f44f46127b4ee4</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T07:16:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261126-unacceptable-major-economies-push-back-against-new-us-tariffs--d6837466366d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261126-unacceptable-major-economies-push-back-against-new-us-tariffs" /><summary type="html">China, the European Union and other major trading partners on Thursday criticised new US tariffs of up to 20 percent proposed by US President Donald Trump after a probe into alleged global overcapacity, raising the prospect of fresh trade tensions with allies and rivals alike.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Powerful US storm forces historic postponement of New York's Thanksgiving Day Parade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6fc62925151ed5b02ed9929bd01c865255133fcc8ee1bd6d6a83236db618121e</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T01:11:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261126-powerful-us-storm-forces-historic-postponement-of-thanksgiving-day-parade-in-new-york--c61a463d7d7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261126-powerful-us-storm-forces-historic-postponement-of-thanksgiving-day-parade-in-new-york" /><summary type="html">A powerful storm forecast to bring fierce winds and heavy rain to the northeastern United States has forced the unprecedented postponement of the city's 100th annual Thanksgiving Day Parade, with the event rescheduled for Saturday. Officials warned that Thursday's conditions could bring down tree limbs and power lines, while posing a safety risk to the parade's giant balloons and the crowds below.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>New US tariffs: 'Trump lashing out really indiscriminately', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be7bb9e75d4b94b6af813fecb4972cc0b0dda2ed491ae8afafddbcd7b888fc27</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T22:13:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261125-new-us-tariffs-trump-lashing-out-really-indiscriminately-expert-says--e101abdd1c03.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261125-new-us-tariffs-trump-lashing-out-really-indiscriminately-expert-says" /><summary type="html">The United States on Wednesday unveiled proposed tariffs on 14 economies including the European Union and China, after a months-long probe into alleged excess production.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>New US tariffs: 'Trump lashing out really indiscriminately', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85ea455ee1e85c0c76a102adcb5897dd450113c348e8bc53f8a6bf3aa959d47f</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T22:11:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/new-us-tariffs-trump-lashing-out-really-indiscriminately-expert-says--acea06a7285b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/new-us-tariffs-trump-lashing-out-really-indiscriminately-expert-says" /><summary type="html">The United States on Wednesday unveiled proposed tariffs on 14 economies including the European Union and China, after a months-long probe into alleged excess production. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Dean Baker, senior economist at the Centre for Economic and Policy Research, says that "there has to be some mechanism for better coordinating China's involvement in the world trade system and ideally the US, the EU, Canada would have a common front, some clear ground rules that we could agree to, that China could agree to, to be mutually beneficial. It's not a step in that direction, we have President Trump lashing out really indiscriminately. It's very hard to see his approach being very productive".</summary></entry><entry><title>US Army detonates lead explosives in Iowa despite contamination fears</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5359a21c7c15f3fbefefb135d5c3146fb912bfa1a544bbcdf4b8ae0d10ad938</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T16:08:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261125-us-army-detonates-lead-explosives-iowa-despite-community-backlash--881956a58273.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261125-us-army-detonates-lead-explosives-iowa-despite-community-backlash" /><summary type="html">The US Army on Wednesday blew up 5 tons of lead-based explosives at an ammunition plant in Iowa despite community backlash over fears of environmental contamination. The detonation was postponed three times, but got the green light after a federal appeals court this week found the US Environmental Protection Agency adequately incorporated safeguards to minimise the dispersal of lead dust.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'We need to stop the war in Iran': US Congresswoman Pramila Jayapal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e5d26e3aca3ba3dd924e0d0ee819b014691d1e9439eb1aa33200b720402abcd</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T15:46:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261125-we-need-to-stop-the-war-in-iran-us-congresswoman-pramila-jayapal--819b76c179be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261125-we-need-to-stop-the-war-in-iran-us-congresswoman-pramila-jayapal" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Democratic Congresswoman Pramila Jayapal laid out her priorities for the new Congress: ending the war in Iran, tackling the cost-of-living crisis, curbing political corruption and holding the Trump administration accountable for its immigration crackdown. She also called for the "complete" dismantling of the US federal immigration agency ICE and backed an end to US military funding for Israel.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Trump announces new tariffs on EU, China despite US midterms defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:faa6f8e5291831d2984f4393650665b41a58806a516e09057310b870c0205013</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T14:38:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261125-trump-announces-new-tariffs-eu-china-despite-us-midterms-defeat--92ccd49b5a64.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261125-trump-announces-new-tariffs-eu-china-despite-us-midterms-defeat" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump's administration on Wednesday reignited global trade tensions by proposing new tariffs on some of the largest US trading partners, including the EU, Japan and Taiwan. China could be slapped with a 20 percent tariff, a senior official said. The announcement came weeks after a cost-of-living crisis landed the Republicans a sweeping defeat in the US midterms.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Cyberattack exposes unclassified information from CIA system, US media reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18d221c41486f8d3e80fe6b445f91c053a9463274a0c972b5cf01ec8a56f995f</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T10:48:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261125-cyberattack-exposes-unclassified-information-from-cia-system-us-media-reports--88d820aa74ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261125-cyberattack-exposes-unclassified-information-from-cia-system-us-media-reports" /><summary type="html">A recently discovered hack on a CIA analysis system exposed some unclassified information, US media reported on Tuesday. The breach is the latest in a series of cyber attacks that have targeted US government departments and major companies in recent weeks.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>New York jury convicts Huawei of stealing trade secrets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7a607241da8b5be36747b99a61fb6d3cde1c61d27e9730ef8ddf9fbd16d4093</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T23:31:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-new-york-jury-convicts-huawei-of-stealing-trade-secrets--9763c33e7309.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-new-york-jury-convicts-huawei-of-stealing-trade-secrets" /><summary type="html">A New York jury on Tuesday found Chinese telecom giant Huawei guilty of stealing trade secrets and other criminal offences, but acquitted it of a racketeering conspiracy and obstruction of justice. The verdict followed a three-month trial in New York in a case that adds to longstanding US efforts to curb Huawei's operations over alleged threats to national security.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Tech executives' investment in Trump 'clearly paying off' as Huang reinstated at Nvidia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe78aefe9dd1e0288d63a6e0893dc8723c88cb05364474ea8712ea04159bd870</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T21:57:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tech-executives-investment-in-trump-clearly-paying-off-as-huang-reinstated-at-nvidia--08418866b8df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tech-executives-investment-in-trump-clearly-paying-off-as-huang-reinstated-at-nvidia" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, The Hill Senior Technology Reporter Miranda Nazzaro says that the reinstatement of Jensen Huang at Nvidia represents "the culmination of a two-year push of tech executives to get closer to President Trump and their investment in the president is clearly paying off".</summary></entry><entry><title>'Quid pro quo’: Nvidia too big to fail or ‘too close to personal interest of people around Trump’?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2ba0a5dca97a554e2dc382821ca9ff3047827f207f142d772ee5424191d066d</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T21:43:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/quid-pro-quo-nvidia-too-big-to-fail-or-too-close-to-personal-interest-of-people-around-trump--c77d6b4d7d29.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/quid-pro-quo-nvidia-too-big-to-fail-or-too-close-to-personal-interest-of-people-around-trump" /><summary type="html">Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Bernard Benhamou, Secretary General of the Institute of Digital Sovereignty and Senior Lecturer in Internet Governance at Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne University. What does Jensen Huang's return to Nvidia mean for Trump, Lutnick, the US, the AI industry and China? Describing Huang as “the global banker of the AI industry”, Benhamou explains: “He is the visionary, he is the banker. He's not only the chip maker.” He also warns of the repercussions of Donald Trump's decision to reinstate the Nvidia CEO, with congressional and judicial scrutiny looming. “It's far from over. It's just the beginning.”</summary></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang's Nvidia comeback sends AI videos into overdrive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37a9ee775251c38e9b4a62a3afcd64bee5a4bbd6e5a7d194d536910c49872490</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T21:28:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261124-jensen-huang-s-nvidia-comeback-sends-ai-videos-into-overdrive--7cae4d0e07af.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261124-jensen-huang-s-nvidia-comeback-sends-ai-videos-into-overdrive" /><summary type="html">Just 11 days after resigning as Nvidia CEO, Jensen Huang's return has unleashed a fresh wave of AI-generated videos. But the internet has changed its tune: while last week's memes mocked Huang, many now celebrate his comeback. One viral video purportedly showing him dancing is actually AI-manipulated footage of a basketball coach from 2016. From humiliation to hero worship, the technology Nvidia helped popularise is rewriting the narrative surrounding its own CEO, as Vedika Bahl explains.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Did Nvidia knowingly send chips to China 'cutout'? Was there 'pay-to-play' involving Trump, Lutnick?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:574e216e6ae9b4a7c17a1b22fa1f35f1e4c8545b9b4291a56cc7b35c46dc0afb</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T21:20:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261124-did-nvidia-knowingly-send-chips-to-china-cutout-was-there-pay-to-play-involving-trump-lutni--aeb32db87e92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261124-did-nvidia-knowingly-send-chips-to-china-cutout-was-there-pay-to-play-involving-trump-lutnick" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Andrew Weissmann, Professor of Practice at NYU School of Law and a former federal prosecutor known for leading major Department of Justice (DOJ) and FBI investigations. Professor Weissmann joins us to discuss the legal and ethical questions surrounding the Trump administration's dealings with chipmaker Nvidia following the reinstatement of Jensen Huang as president and CEO.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>The Bukele method: Will Salvadoran leader's strong-arm tactics work for Haiti?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26666eab0b3d6262c7e20ed6c71fb5b9d01979c232898fca61185571bbc0a4ed</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T19:59:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261124-the-bukele-method-will-salvadoran-leader-s-strong-arm-tactics-work-for-haiti--28cf4ba3b953.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261124-the-bukele-method-will-salvadoran-leader-s-strong-arm-tactics-work-for-haiti" /><summary type="html">Haitians are hailing the Bukele method. Citizens of the Americas' poorest nation are cheering the Salvadoran president’s "shoot first, ask questions later" method of dealing with the gangs that have overrun their country for the past six years. Can the police force deployed actually restore law and order? We ask about the latest in a decades-long list of efforts by the international community to support Haiti.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Car bomb destroys buildings in central Colombian city</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6cfcd8dbfd84ad27a4289205a821accad038e360306a91842f9c31b8e8d8f3ee</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T19:27:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/car-bomb-destroys-buildings-in-central-colombian-city--7617558acf7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/car-bomb-destroys-buildings-in-central-colombian-city" /><summary type="html">A car bomb detonated in the central Colombian city of Villavicencio on Monday, destroying a local governor's office and surrounding buildings, President Abelardo de la Espriella said. The right-wing leader has conducted a major crackdown on the country's drug trade, in response to left-wing FARC rebels who have stepped up attacks over the past two years. FRANCE 24's Daniel Whittington reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Colombia president says 'all hostages rescued' from supermarket siege</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25709cfec8c06db6b37be3d8cf02bdb3efb07d5fab6537f0da9b24543f1a75b8</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T17:35:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-hostages-supermarket-colombia-cartagena-flights--23f238675216.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-hostages-supermarket-colombia-cartagena-flights" /><summary type="html">Colombia's President President Abelardo de la Espriella said on Wednesday that around 20 hostages being held by gunmen in a supermarket in Cartagena had been rescued. Security forces earlier entered the scene of the hours-long siege after several explosions were heard.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Huang returns as Nvidia CEO in sudden reversal after Trump intervention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35d995676f05c911d2d104c069f4867d764079ac800b558ce15aa999dc86c1ab</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T12:19:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261124-huang-returns-as-nvidia-ceo-in-sudden-reversal-after-trump-intervention--566d5895c043.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261124-huang-returns-as-nvidia-ceo-in-sudden-reversal-after-trump-intervention" /><summary type="html">Nvidia reinstated Jensen Huang as CEO on Monday under pressure from US President Donald Trump, drawing approval/plaudits/cheers  from Wall Street and criticism from US lawmakers. The sudden reversal was the latest twist in the fallout from Huang’s admission that he had an affair with a woman suspected of being a Chinese spy.</summary></entry><entry><title>Huang’s return to Nvidia calms markets but fears of an AI bubble still run deep</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc6c4265c7773a62aa67bca893fda7e55e0c6d8dc5e54a09c222b38d7fb8e482</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T07:15:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-jensen-huang-s-return-has-calmed-markets-but-fears-of-an-ai-bubble-still-run-deep--4522ba2897b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-jensen-huang-s-return-has-calmed-markets-but-fears-of-an-ai-bubble-still-run-deep" /><summary type="html">Nvidia's decision to bring back Jensen Huang as CEO pushed the AI computing company's stocks up more than 30 percent Monday. But the model of circular financing increasingly underwriting the AI boom still has some analysts worried that the party can't last forever.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US flew surveillance drone over Mexico to help capture top drug lord</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eff2fa21ced12bc86183e40eae399837a60445d141d2cb01cdbdba6aa4a687e9</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T02:09:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-us-flew-surveillance-drone-over-mexico-to-help-capture-top-drug-lord--342d551a758c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-us-flew-surveillance-drone-over-mexico-to-help-capture-top-drug-lord" /><summary type="html">Mexican officials say the United States flew a surveillance drone over Mexican territory to help locate and capture one of the country's most wanted drug traffickers. The operation led to the arrest of Fausto Isidro Meza Flores, known as 'El Chapo Isidro'.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump backs Nvidia boss's return but top Democrat vows probe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac7c07661352c7c65250c29f191a8fbbd922b5e24013cb97a8c4a0e79a889db4</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T19:53:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-backs-nvidia-boss-s-return-but-top-democrat-vows-probe--0b7b3a362597.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-backs-nvidia-boss-s-return-but-top-democrat-vows-probe" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump praised Nvidia's decision Monday to reinstate Jensen Huang as chief executive, as top Senate Democrat Chuck Schumer vowed to investigate potential wrongdoing amid mounting national security concerns. Trump also posted a doctored version of the famous photograph of him raising his fist after surviving a 2024 assassination attempt, replacing himself with Huang, who brandished a red bra beneath an Nvidia flag. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Maintain control': UN chief calls for creation of global AI safety framework within a year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48050c1445b8732b817836aeb1c3a4b21da6093354e4b2104bb95882b88ea2fe</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T19:06:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-un-chief-antonio-guterres-calls-for-global-ai-safety-framework-within-a-year--b8cbcdfbe9c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-un-chief-antonio-guterres-calls-for-global-ai-safety-framework-within-a-year" /><summary type="html">UN chief Antonio Guterres on Monday urged countries to agree on the creation of a global framework for managing the dangers posed by artificial intelligence within one year. Speaking at a summit in Barbados, he warned that taming the technology is vital if humanity is to stay in charge of its own future.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Democrats vow probe after Trump presses Huang's return as Nvidia CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff2efe1108f68f6f5da02e67e3c12e6b8266367b97b594ba83a8c8c421231b94</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:06:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-nvidia-board-reinstates-disgraced-jensen-huang-as-ceo-president-says--1a69aac9014a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-nvidia-board-reinstates-disgraced-jensen-huang-as-ceo-president-says" /><summary type="html">Nvidia on ⁠Monday said it ​was immediately reinstating disgraced tech titan Jensen Huang as its chief executive, marking an extraordinary reversal ​under pressure from US President Donald Trump, who said he had directly intervened within Nvidia's board. Democratic Senate leader Chuck Schumer vowed to investigate potential wrongdoing by "anybody selling out our national security for financial gain".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Out of control': ICE agents make arrests at Seattle airport in 'horrific' scene</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:088436683c969b120cdce57d2565e14df0176b82ab3986e602e9c60f1b4a1e3f</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T12:11:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-out-of-control-ice-agents-make-arrests-at-seattle-airport-in-horrific-scene--3d2cfac9c9ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-out-of-control-ice-agents-make-arrests-at-seattle-airport-in-horrific-scene" /><summary type="html">The governor of Washington state called US federal immigration agents "out of control" after they arrested two people at Seattle's main airport on Saturday. ICE officers have conducted raids across the United States, part of President Donald Trump's immigration crackdown which has forged ahead despite a rebuke by voters at this month's midterms.</summary></entry><entry><title>Alice Huang had contact with China spy agency during affair with Nvidia boss, New York Times reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5baef55543b9feedbe6882787a65a83bf17182aee92d22fdf98a1291e26b40a6</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:48:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-alice-huang-had-contact-with-china-spy-agency-during-affair-with-nvidia-boss-nyt-reports--c1a1f982d978.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-alice-huang-had-contact-with-china-spy-agency-during-affair-with-nvidia-boss-nyt-reports" /><summary type="html">Alice Huang, who is alleged to have been spying for Chinese intelligence during her affair with former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang, was in contact with China's Ministry of State Security until autumn 2026, the New York Times reported Monday, citing people with knowledge of US intelligence reports.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Democrat Hubbard wins North Carolina recount, clinching historic House majority</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93e11207c77bacb58e323998add3beffe9c71eee7d151fe9a1becd5ed8ee1c2d</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T20:16:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261122-democrat-hubbard-wins-north-carolina-recount-clinching-historic-house-majority--58e941bd0d61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261122-democrat-hubbard-wins-north-carolina-recount-clinching-historic-house-majority" /><summary type="html">Democrat Chuck Hubbard was elected to the US House of Representatives from North Carolina on Sunday after defeating veteran Republican Virginia Foxx, who chairs the powerful House Rules Committee. His victory gave Democrats their best general election result in decades, winning at least 258 seats in the 2026 US midterms.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>FBI criminal database hacked</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:543247ea107e5aebadb4b64a91df3d382af7410ac970920343e58c3b371104a7</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T17:23:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/fbi-criminal-database-hacked--0e998fd7b8f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/fbi-criminal-database-hacked" /><summary type="html">The FBI is investigating a reported major cyberattack targeting its national law enforcement database, the National Crime Information Center (NCIC), which holds sensitive criminal justice records, including information on fugitives, missing persons, criminal histories and stolen property. President Donald Trump said he had just been briefed on the incident, describing it as “not good”. FRANCE 24’s Fraser Jackson reports from Washington DC.</summary></entry></feed>
